<h2>Common Action Patterns</h2>

<p>
    Here are some common patterns for combining actions:
</p>

<h3>Simple Email</h3>
<ul>
    <li>One action: Send Email</li>
    <li>Use for: Welcome emails, reminders, notifications</li>
</ul>

<h3>Create and Notify</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Action 1: Create Record (renewal, task, etc.)</li>
    <li>Action 2: Send Email (notify about the created record)</li>
    <li>Use for: Creating renewals and notifying clients</li>
</ul>

<h3>Try Primary, Fallback to Secondary</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Action 1: Send Email (primary method) - Stop on Success</li>
    <li>Action 2: Send Email (fallback method)</li>
    <li>Use for: Contacting clients via preferred method, with backup</li>
</ul>

