<h2>Best Practices</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Keep actions focused</strong> – Each action should do one thing well</li>
    <li><strong>Order matters</strong> – Place actions in the order they need to execute</li>
    <li><strong>Handle errors gracefully</strong> – Use "Stop on Failure" for critical actions</li>
    <li><strong>Test thoroughly</strong> – Always test actions with real data before publishing</li>
    <li><strong>Map parameters clearly</strong> – Ensure all required template fields are mapped</li>
    <li><strong>Document complex flows</strong> – If actions have complex logic, document it in the agent description</li>
    <li><strong>Update when templates change</strong> – Keep action mappings in sync with email templates</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual checklist showing best practices with icons: focus icon, order icon, error handling icon, testing icon. -->

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

<h3>Email Not Sending</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Verify email integration is configured (Microsoft Graph, etc.)</li>
    <li>Check that all required template fields are mapped to parameters</li>
    <li>Ensure parameters have values when the agent runs</li>
    <li>Review error messages for specific issues</li>
</ul>

<h3>Wrong Data in Email</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Check parameter mappings—ensure fields are mapped to the correct parameters</li>
    <li>Verify parameters are pulling the right data from the page</li>
    <li>Test with different clients/policies to see if the issue is consistent</li>
</ul>

<h3>Actions Not Running in Order</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Verify actions are in the correct order in the action list</li>
    <li>Check "Stop on Failure" settings—an early failure might prevent later actions</li>
    <li>Review action execution logs if available</li>
</ul>

